 "about": [
  "What an acquisition of an http source may name, docs/adr/0040-path-templates-and-links-on-an-http-source.md: a path among the configured paths and templates, or a link under the endpoint; and which configured paths are templates the rules admit.",
  "Read by adapter-http (adapters/httpsource, ParseRequest and admits), which is what refuses a request before a connection is made, and by the engine (go/http_request_target.go, tokenStepAdmits), which refuses the same requests before a token is obtained for one, each in a test of its own.",
  "Each case names the rule it is written for: an accepted case stands on the accepting side of that rule, and a refused case breaks it. Every rule has a case on each side. An accepted case gives the path sent under the endpoint and the query sent, byte for byte; adapter-http's test holds the request it forms to both.",
  "endpoint, paths and methods are those every case is read under, unless the case gives its own. padLinkTo: the request's link is extended with \"a\" until it is that many bytes long, and an accepted case's rawQuery by the same \"a\"s.",
  "Written by hand from ADR-0040, not computed by an implementation. Every name, host and identifier is invented."
 ],
